# server/public/audio/ (the actual generated .mp3 files) is deliberately
# NOT gitignored, despite being regenerable — Render's deploy only has
# what's in git, and the server serves these as static files, so without
# them every lesson silently falls back to on-device TTS in production
# (a real gap hit once already: internal testing against the deployed
# backend had no working Hindi narration at all). Only ~16MB across 378
# files today; revisit with real cloud storage (S3/R2/Supabase Storage)
# once the audio set is large enough that committing it to git stops
# being the pragmatic choice — not yet.

